// EXPECT-ERROR: Expected type identifier, got: :
// Design guard: a trait has NO colon before its parent list.
//
// Koral spells trait inheritance `trait Child Parent1 and Parent2 { ... }`.
// `trait Child: Parent` is a syntax error, not a legal alternative spelling.
//
// This pins a fact that was stated wrongly in a review note ("`trait X: Any` is
// syntactically legal") and would have justified keeping name special-casing for
// `Any` in the supertrait position. There is no supertrait position in which a
// colon appears, so `Any` there is just an ordinary trait name.

trait Foo {
    m(self) Int;
};

trait Bar: Foo {
    n(self) Int;
};

let main() Int = {
    return 0;
};
